ACA 2025 is an in-person conference. There is no online participation
registration option and there will be no broadcasting of the sessions.
Participants who cannot participate in person for reasons not under their
control (e.g., visa problems) can give a talk online, but the technical setup
is not guaranteed to allow bidirectional communication.  This means, for
example, that the session chair should repeat questions from the audience.
Also, every special session should have no more than 20% of online talks.
This is because, in our experience, blocks with many online talks tend to have
low attendance by in-person participants.
====
So, it is possible to have an online talk if necessary, but the talks will not
be broadcasted. 
